# Source of truth

`AGENTS.md` at this repo's root is authoritative — UI intent, API integration
rules, role-awareness, testing conventions, and which Notion sections to
fetch for actual UI content, derived from ADR-024/ADR-020/ADR-028 and
Section 11. Read it before generating or modifying any component. This file
adds Cursor-specific behaviors only.

# Working behaviors specific to this repo

- **Notion MCP access is read-only by token config, and must never be
  treated as writable regardless of what's asked.** Fetch fresh each
  session per AGENTS.md's section list; treat content as authoritative,
  flag disagreement rather than silently deviating.
- **Never hand-write a type for a backend request/response shape.** If a
  needed type doesn't exist under `src/api/generated/`, say so and stop —
  regenerate from the live OpenAPI spec (AGENTS.md §3) rather than stubbing an
  interface that will silently drift from the real contract.
- **Before adding a new UI dependency** (a component library, a date picker,
  a chart library), check whether shadcn/ui + the already-approved libraries
  (react-force-graph, D3, recharts-equivalent per Section 11) cover it first.
- **When building a new list/table view, generate pagination and sort
  controls in the same pass as the initial layout** — not as a follow-up.
  This was a real gap caught late once already; don't repeat it.
- **When a component renders anything from the API response involving a
  victim, an IPC/BNS citation, or role-restricted data, explicitly call out
  in your response which AGENTS.md rule applies** (victim-identity stripping,
  `formatLegalSection`, role-gated fetch) — don't apply it silently in a way
  that's easy to miss in review.
- **Flag, don't silently fix, any existing code that contradicts
  `AGENTS.md`** (e.g., `localStorage` used for a token, a hand-written API
  type). Point it out and ask before changing it.